{"candidate_ids": [], "chapter_number": 113, "locally_named_context_leads": [], "no_ambient_hypotheses_inferred": true, "omitted_proof_line_count": 0, "possible_scope_prose_line_numbers": [], "previous_draft_artifact_hint": null, "proof_free_source_lines": [{"line": 55, "tex": "\\section{Stacks}"}, {"line": 56, "tex": "\\label{section-stacks}"}, {"line": 58, "tex": "\\noindent"}, {"line": 59, "tex": "We have a chapter on (abstract) stacks, see"}, {"line": 60, "tex": "Stacks, Section \\ref{stacks-section-introduction}."}, {"line": 61, "tex": "It would be nice if"}, {"line": 62, "tex": "\\begin{enumerate}"}, {"line": 63, "tex": "\\item improve the discussion on ``stackyfication'',"}, {"line": 64, "tex": "\\item give examples of stackyfication,"}, {"line": 65, "tex": "\\item more examples in general,"}, {"line": 66, "tex": "\\item improve the discussion of gerbes."}, {"line": 67, "tex": "\\end{enumerate}"}, {"line": 68, "tex": "Example result which has not been added yet: Given a sheaf of abelian"}, {"line": 69, "tex": "groups $\\mathcal{F}$"}, {"line": 70, "tex": "over $\\mathcal{C}$ the set of equivalence classes of gerbes banded by"}, {"line": 71, "tex": "$\\mathcal{F}$ is bijective to $H^2(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{F})$."}], "schema": "maththm.phase2.chapter-section-input.v1", "scope_extraction_error_requires_review": null, "section_end_line": 73, "section_label": "section-stacks", "section_start_line": 55, "section_title": "Stacks", "source_file": "desirables.tex", "source_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_scope_events_unadjudicated": []}
{"candidate_ids": [], "chapter_number": 113, "locally_named_context_leads": [], "no_ambient_hypotheses_inferred": true, "omitted_proof_line_count": 0, "possible_scope_prose_line_numbers": [], "previous_draft_artifact_hint": null, "proof_free_source_lines": [{"line": 74, "tex": "\\section{Simplicial methods}"}, {"line": 75, "tex": "\\label{section-simplicial}"}, {"line": 77, "tex": "\\noindent"}, {"line": 78, "tex": "We have a chapter on simplicial methods, see"}, {"line": 79, "tex": "Simplicial, Section \\ref{simplicial-section-introduction}."}, {"line": 80, "tex": "This has to be reviewed and improved. The discussion of"}, {"line": 81, "tex": "the relationship between simplicial homotopy (also known as"}, {"line": 82, "tex": "combinatorial homotopy) and Kan complexes should be improved upon."}, {"line": 83, "tex": "There is a chapter on simplicial spaces, see"}, {"line": 84, "tex": "Simplicial Spaces, Section \\ref{spaces-simplicial-section-introduction}."}, {"line": 85, "tex": "This chapter briefly discusses"}, {"line": 86, "tex": "simplicial topological spaces, simplicial sites, and simplicial topoi."}, {"line": 87, "tex": "We can further develop ``simplicial algebraic geometry'' to discuss"}, {"line": 88, "tex": "simplicial schemes (or simplicial algebraic spaces, or"}, {"line": 89, "tex": "simplicial algebraic stacks) and treat geometric questions, their cohomology,"}, {"line": 90, "tex": "etc."}], "schema": "maththm.phase2.chapter-section-input.v1", "scope_extraction_error_requires_review": null, "section_end_line": 92, "section_label": "section-simplicial", "section_start_line": 74, "section_title": "Simplicial methods", "source_file": "desirables.tex", "source_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_scope_events_unadjudicated": []}
{"candidate_ids": [], "chapter_number": 113, "locally_named_context_leads": [], "no_ambient_hypotheses_inferred": true, "omitted_proof_line_count": 0, "possible_scope_prose_line_numbers": [], "previous_draft_artifact_hint": null, "proof_free_source_lines": [{"line": 93, "tex": "\\section{Cohomology of schemes}"}, {"line": 94, "tex": "\\label{section-schemes-cohomology}"}, {"line": 96, "tex": "\\noindent"}, {"line": 97, "tex": "There is already a chapter on cohomology of quasi-coherent sheaves, see"}, {"line": 98, "tex": "Cohomology of Schemes, Section \\ref{coherent-section-introduction}."}, {"line": 99, "tex": "We have a chapter discussing the derived category of"}, {"line": 100, "tex": "quasi-coherent sheaves on a scheme, see"}, {"line": 101, "tex": "Derived Categories of Schemes, Section \\ref{perfect-section-introduction}."}, {"line": 102, "tex": "We have a chapter discussing duality for Noetherian schemes"}, {"line": 103, "tex": "and relative duality for morphisms of schemes, see"}, {"line": 104, "tex": "Duality for Schemes, Section \\ref{duality-section-introduction}."}, {"line": 105, "tex": "We also have chapters on \\'etale cohomology of schemes and on"}, {"line": 106, "tex": "crystalline cohomology of schemes. But most of the material in these"}, {"line": 107, "tex": "chapters is very basic and a lot more could/should be added there."}], "schema": "maththm.phase2.chapter-section-input.v1", "scope_extraction_error_requires_review": null, "section_end_line": 109, "section_label": "section-schemes-cohomology", "section_start_line": 93, "section_title": "Cohomology of schemes", "source_file": "desirables.tex", "source_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_scope_events_unadjudicated": []}
{"candidate_ids": [], "chapter_number": 113, "locally_named_context_leads": [], "no_ambient_hypotheses_inferred": true, "omitted_proof_line_count": 0, "possible_scope_prose_line_numbers": [], "previous_draft_artifact_hint": null, "proof_free_source_lines": [{"line": 110, "tex": "\\section{Deformation theory \\`a la Schlessinger}"}, {"line": 111, "tex": "\\label{section-deformation-schlessinger}"}, {"line": 113, "tex": "\\noindent"}, {"line": 114, "tex": "We have a chapter on this material, see"}, {"line": 115, "tex": "Formal Deformation Theory, Section \\ref{formal-defos-section-introduction}."}, {"line": 116, "tex": "We have a chapter discussing examples of the general theory, see"}, {"line": 117, "tex": "Deformation Problems, Section \\ref{examples-defos-section-introduction}."}, {"line": 118, "tex": "We have a chapter, see"}, {"line": 119, "tex": "Deformation Theory, Section \\ref{defos-section-introduction}"}, {"line": 120, "tex": "which discusses deformations of rings (and modules),"}, {"line": 121, "tex": "deformations of ringed spaces (and sheaves of modules),"}, {"line": 122, "tex": "deformations of ringed topoi (and sheaves of modules)."}, {"line": 123, "tex": "In this chapter we use the naive cotangent complex"}, {"line": 124, "tex": "to describe obstructions, first order deformations, and"}, {"line": 125, "tex": "infinitesimal automorphisms. This material has found some"}, {"line": 126, "tex": "applications to algebraicity of moduli stacks in later chapters."}, {"line": 127, "tex": "There is also a chapter discussing the full cotangent complex, see"}, {"line": 128, "tex": "Cotangent, Section \\ref{cotangent-section-introduction}."}], "schema": "maththm.phase2.chapter-section-input.v1", "scope_extraction_error_requires_review": null, "section_end_line": 130, "section_label": "section-deformation-schlessinger", "section_start_line": 110, "section_title": "Deformation theory \\`a la Schlessinger", "source_file": "desirables.tex", "source_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_scope_events_unadjudicated": []}
{"candidate_ids": [], "chapter_number": 113, "locally_named_context_leads": [], "no_ambient_hypotheses_inferred": true, "omitted_proof_line_count": 0, "possible_scope_prose_line_numbers": [], "previous_draft_artifact_hint": null, "proof_free_source_lines": [{"line": 131, "tex": "\\section{Definition of algebraic stacks}"}, {"line": 132, "tex": "\\label{section-definition-algebraic-stacks}"}, {"line": 134, "tex": "\\noindent"}, {"line": 135, "tex": "An algebraic stack is a stack in groupoids over the category of schemes"}, {"line": 136, "tex": "with the fppf topology that has a diagonal representable by algebraic"}, {"line": 137, "tex": "spaces and is the target of a surjective smooth morphism from a scheme."}, {"line": 138, "tex": "See Algebraic Stacks, Section \\ref{algebraic-section-algebraic-stacks}."}, {"line": 139, "tex": "A ``Deligne-Mumford stack'' is an algebraic stack for which there exists"}, {"line": 140, "tex": "a scheme and a surjective \\'etale morphism from that scheme to it"}, {"line": 141, "tex": "as in the paper \\cite{DM} of Deligne and Mumford, see"}, {"line": 142, "tex": "Algebraic Stacks, Definition \\ref{algebraic-definition-deligne-mumford}."}, {"line": 143, "tex": "We will reserve the term ``Artin stack'' for a stack such as in the papers by"}, {"line": 144, "tex": "Artin, see \\cite{ArtinI}, \\cite{ArtinII}, and \\cite{ArtinVersal}."}, {"line": 145, "tex": "A possible definition is that an Artin stack is an algebraic stack"}, {"line": 146, "tex": "$\\mathcal{X}$ over a locally Noetherian scheme $S$ such that"}, {"line": 147, "tex": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to S$ is"}, {"line": 148, "tex": "locally of finite type\\footnote{Namely, these are exactly the algebraic"}, {"line": 149, "tex": "stacks over $S$ satisfying Artin's axioms [-1], [0], [1], [2], [3], [4], [5]"}, {"line": 150, "tex": "of Artin's Axioms, Section \\ref{artin-section-axioms}.}."}], "schema": "maththm.phase2.chapter-section-input.v1", "scope_extraction_error_requires_review": null, "section_end_line": 152, "section_label": "section-definition-algebraic-stacks", "section_start_line": 131, "section_title": "Definition of algebraic stacks", "source_file": "desirables.tex", "source_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_scope_events_unadjudicated": []}
{"candidate_ids": [], "chapter_number": 113, "locally_named_context_leads": [], "no_ambient_hypotheses_inferred": true, "omitted_proof_line_count": 0, "possible_scope_prose_line_numbers": [], "previous_draft_artifact_hint": null, "proof_free_source_lines": [{"line": 153, "tex": "\\section{Examples of schemes, algebraic spaces, algebraic stacks}"}, {"line": 154, "tex": "\\label{section-examples-stacks}"}, {"line": 156, "tex": "\\noindent"}, {"line": 157, "tex": "The Stacks project currently contains two chapters discussing"}, {"line": 158, "tex": "moduli stacks and their properties, see"}, {"line": 159, "tex": "Moduli Stacks, Section \\ref{moduli-section-introduction} and"}, {"line": 160, "tex": "Moduli of Curves, Section \\ref{moduli-curves-section-introduction}."}, {"line": 161, "tex": "Over time we intend to add more, for example:"}, {"line": 162, "tex": "\\begin{enumerate}"}, {"line": 163, "tex": "\\item $\\mathcal{A}_g$,"}, {"line": 164, "tex": "i.e., principally polarized abelian schemes of genus $g$,"}, {"line": 165, "tex": "\\item $\\mathcal{A}_1 = \\mathcal{M}_{1, 1}$, i.e.,"}, {"line": 166, "tex": "$1$-pointed smooth projective genus $1$ curves,"}, {"line": 167, "tex": "\\item $\\mathcal{M}_{g, n}$, i.e., smooth projective genus $g$-curves"}, {"line": 168, "tex": "with $n$ pairwise distinct labeled points,"}, {"line": 169, "tex": "\\item $\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}_{g, n}$, i.e.,"}, {"line": 170, "tex": "stable $n$-pointed nodal projective genus $g$-curves,"}, {"line": 171, "tex": "\\item $\\SheafHom_S(\\mathcal{X}, \\mathcal{Y})$, moduli of morphisms"}, {"line": 172, "tex": "(with suitable conditions on the stacks $\\mathcal{X}$, $\\mathcal{Y}$"}, {"line": 173, "tex": "and the base scheme $S$),"}, {"line": 174, "tex": "\\item $\\textit{Bun}_G(X) = \\SheafHom_S(X, BG)$, the stack of $G$-bundles"}, {"line": 175, "tex": "of the geometric Langlands programme (with suitable conditions on the scheme"}, {"line": 176, "tex": "$X$, the group scheme $G$, and the base scheme $S$),"}, {"line": 177, "tex": "\\item $\\Picardstack_{\\mathcal{X}/S}$, i.e., the Picard stack associated"}, {"line": 178, "tex": "to an algebraic stack over a base scheme (or space)."}, {"line": 179, "tex": "\\end{enumerate}"}, {"line": 180, "tex": "More generally, the Stacks project is somewhat"}, {"line": 181, "tex": "lacking in geometrically meaningful examples."}], "schema": "maththm.phase2.chapter-section-input.v1", "scope_extraction_error_requires_review": null, "section_end_line": 183, "section_label": "section-examples-stacks", "section_start_line": 153, "section_title": "Examples of schemes, algebraic spaces, algebraic stacks", "source_file": "desirables.tex", "source_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_scope_events_unadjudicated": []}
